-- `l4 batch` and the decision service write a default into a module of their own
-- as text, after the file's last section, and read its names again there. A name
-- that two sections define means the one in its own section where the default is
-- written, and the last section's (or, when the last section does not define it,
-- nothing the author wrote) there, so the same input would give two answers, with
-- no error. It is refused for an exported rule, like a name that is defined in a
-- section and at the top level (typically-default-resolved-elsewhere.l4)
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W10, §4.4, review F1). Written with its
-- section, the name says which it is.

§ `Rates`
    -- ERROR: a section input's default naming `phi`, which `§ Other` also
    -- defines; an exported rule below reads it
    GIVEN scale IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS 1)

GIVETH A NUMBER
phi MEANS 8

-- ERROR: an exported rule's input default naming `phi`
@export default Pay
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
pay MEANS (base TIMES rate) PLUS scale

-- Fine: the same, with the section named. This rule does not read `scale`.
@export Pay, with the section named
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (`Rates`.phi PLUS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`pay in the section` MEANS base TIMES rate

-- Fine: two definitions of one name in the same section, for different types,
-- resolve the same way in both places.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
size MEANS n PLUS 1

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
size MEANS 100

@export Sized
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (size OF 3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
sized MEANS rate

-- Fine: a rule that is not exported is not written out again by `l4 batch` or
-- the service.
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not exported` MEANS rate

§ `Other`
GIVETH A NUMBER
phi MEANS 9
